-D; SW-1S-2.5/5kg-D; SW-1S-3/6kg-D; SW-1S-4/10kg-D; SW-1S-6/15kg-D; SW-1S-10/20kg-D; SW-1S-15/30kg-D\nsame for SW-1C, SW-1W, SW-1LR, SW-1WR\nER-JR-3/6kg-D; ER-JR-6/15kg-D; ER-JR-15/30kg-D\nPW-II-1/2kg-D \"1/2\"; PW-II-2.5/5kg-D; PW-II-4/10kg-D\n\nminimum_capacity values:\nSingle: ED: 20,40,100,200; ER PLUS & M: 40,100,200 (×2); SW-1 each: 20,20,40,40,100,100,200,200; ER JR: 40,100,200; PW-II: 20,40,100.\nDual: ED: 10,20,40,100; ER PLUS/M: 20,40,100 ×2; SW-1 each: 10,10,20,20,40,40,100,100; ER JR: 20,40,100; PW-II: 10,20,40.\n\nverification_scale_interval:\nSingle: ED: 1,2,5,10; ER PLUS/M: 2,5,10 ×2; SW-1 each: 1,1,2,2,5,5,10,10; ER JR: 2,5,10; PW-II: 1,2,5.\nDual: ED: \"0.5/1\",\"1/2\",\"2/5\",\"5/10\"; ER PLUS/M ×2: \"1/2\",\"2/5\",\"5/10\"; SW-1 each: \"0.5/1\",\"0.5/1\",\"1/2\",\"1/2\",\"2/5\",\"2/5\",\"5/10\",\"5/10\"; ER JR: \"1/2\",\"2/5\",\"5/10\"; PW-II: \"0.5/1\",\"1/2\",\"2/5\".\n\nAlright. Writing final JSON. It'll be long; that's fine. Let me be meticulous.\n\nAlso for model_level structured values: the schema example shows {\"model\": \"G1.6\", \"value\": 2.5} without unit inside (unit at attribute level via unit_symbol). Follow that: {\"attribute\": \"maximum_capacity\", \"unit_symbol\": \"kg\", \"values\": [...]}.\n\nFor dual max values as strings — fine.\n\nOne more consideration: models[] entries — include attributes? Keep minimal: {\"model_id\": \"...\", \"label\": \"...\"}. \n\nAlso should I include characteristics.type_level? I'll add:\n\"type_level\": {\n  \"accuracy_class\": {\"value\": \"III\"},\n  \"power_supply\": {\"value\": \"mains or battery-operated\"}\n}\nHmm \"power_supply\" value is a string list; acceptable as string value. Or power_supply_type. I'll use power_supply_type.\n\nNow the certificate description says \"SW Series\" pattern. Also \"certified pattern: SW Series\".\n\nLet me now write the final JSON carefully.\n\nFor matrix_tables, single table rows: 56 objects {\"model\": \"ED-3kg-S\", \"maximum_capacity\": 3, \"minimum_capacity\": 20, \"verification_scale_interval\": 1}, etc. Dual: strings for max and e.\n\nDescription for tables: \"Merged from the three tables under 'Single-interval instruments' on page 2.\" and dual similarly.\n\nDouble-check the SW-1 single Min values: 20,20,40,40,100,100,200,200 and e 1,1,2,2,5,5,10,10. Yes.\n\nDual SW-1: Max \"1/2\",\"1.5/3\",\"2.5/5\",\"3/6\",\"4/10\",\"6/15\",\"10/20\",\"15/30\"; Min 10,10,20,20,40,40,100,100; e \"0.5/1\",\"0.5/1\",\"1/2\",\"1/2\",\"2/5\",\"2/5\",\"5/10\",\"5/10\". Yes.\n\nER JR dual: Max \"3/6\",\"6/15\",\"15/30\"; Min 20,40,100; e \"1/2\",\"2/5\",\"5/10\". Yes.\nPW-II dual: Max \"1/2\",\"2.5/5\",\"4/10\"; Min 10,20,40; e \"0.5/1\",\"1/2\",\"2/5\". Yes.\nED dual: Max \"1.5/3\",\"3/6\",\"6/15\",\"15/30\"; Min 10,20,40,100; e \"0.5/1\",\"1/2\",\"2/5\",\"5/10\". Yes.\nER PLUS/M dual: Max \"3/6\",\"6/15\",\"15/30\"; Min 20,40,100; e \"1/2\",\"2/5\",\"5/10\". Yes.\n\nNow assemble. I'll write JSON without fences per rule 9.\n\nFor certificate page_total: 4.\n\nproject_number \"T1128/0107\" — it's \"Reference No\". Include.\n\nI'll skip oiml_issuer_id.\n\nAlso include \"scheme\": \"B\" — the MAA. I'm fairly confident MAA = scheme B in OIML-CS.\n\nFinal JSON below. Keep it valid: no trailing commas.",
